# Accepted findings, pinned to an exact file, rule and line.
#
# A fingerprint stops matching the moment the line moves, which is deliberate:
# relocating the key forces someone to look at it again rather than inheriting
# a blanket exemption. Do not replace these with a regex allowlist — a pattern
# broad enough to cover this key is broad enough to hide the next one.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# StaticForms client key (assets/js/main.js, and its minified copy)
#
# Publishable by StaticForms' design: it identifies the form owner from
# browser-side JavaScript, so it is served to every visitor and cannot be kept
# secret. It grants no access to anything we hold.
#
# That is not the same as harmless. Anyone can lift it and submit forms against
# our quota, or send mail that appears to originate from our forms. If that
# starts happening: rotate the key in the StaticForms dashboard, and if it
# recurs, move form delivery behind something that can authenticate the caller.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
assets/js/main.js:generic-api-key:15
assets/js/main.min.js:generic-api-key:1
